title: Genesis 17 – The Covenant of Circumcision
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 17: Abram becomes Abraham, circumcision given as the token of the covenant, a picture of the circumcision of the heart, and Isaac promised.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-17-circumcision.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 17 study
# (posts 6944-6946, 6949). Fixed: "Issac" -> "Isaac"; "Neither incidental or coincidental" -> "nor".

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 17 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 17: The Covenant of Circumcision
sub: Abram Becomes Abraham • The Token • Isaac Promised
refs: Genesis 17:1-27
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== A father of many nations
--- I Am the Almighty God
kicker: vv. 1–2
sub: Walk Before Me, and Be Thou Perfect
scripture: Genesis 17:1-2
p: Now Abram becomes Abraham, decades after his salvation by calling upon the name of the {Lord}, and is given the physical sign of the covenant, circumcision of the flesh. [[Genesis 12:8]]

--- Thy Name Shall Be Abraham
kicker: vv. 3–8
sub: A Father of Many Nations Have I Made Thee
scripture: Genesis 17:3-8 | mark: thy name shall be Abraham; for a father of many nations have I made thee
p: Of the name changes: Abram means “exalted father,” while Abraham, “because I give you to be father of many nations.”

=== The token of the covenant
--- The Token of the Covenant
kicker: vv. 9–11
sub: Every Man Child Among You Shall Be Circumcised
scripture: Genesis 17:9-11 | mark: it shall be a token of the covenant betwixt me and you
p: Of course, this physical act of obedience was a picture of the sealing of a soul by the Holy Spirit to come. The circumcision of the heart.

--- An Everlasting Covenant
kicker: vv. 12–14
sub: He That Is Born in the House, or Bought with Money
scripture: Genesis 17:12-14
p: While the descendants of Abraham kept the circumcision as an ordinance, to remember their covenant with God that brought about Christ Jesus in the flesh, to preserve the seed, even as strangers and bondsmen were added to the nation, in case any forgot God’s promise, the circumcision of the heart, which is found in believers, is to us who are saved a reminder of our salvation and belonging to the body of Christ.

--- The Circumcision of the Heart
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 17:11
fig: Romans 2:28-29 | Romans 2:28-29
fig: Colossians 2:11 | Colossians 2:11

--- The Circumcision of the Heart, continued
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 17:11
fig: Romans 4:10-11 | Romans 4:10-11 | Abraham was saved by faith decades before ([[Genesis 12:8]]; [[Genesis 15:6]]), being yet uncircumcised. The sign was a seal of the righteousness of the faith he already had.

=== Sarah and Isaac
--- Sarah Shall Her Name Be
kicker: vv. 15–16
sub: She Shall Be a Mother of Nations
scripture: Genesis 17:15-16 | mark: Sarah shall her name be
p: Sarai and Sarah both mean “princess,” or a mighty woman, but Sarai is the possessive form, meaning Abram called her “my princess.” As Sarah, now she is just *the* princess. The queen of the multitudes of nations, essentially. We see the name changes by God as something He does, whether it is Jesus renaming the apostles or Saul becoming Paul. Neither incidental nor coincidental. Everything is done for a purpose. [[John 1:42]] [[Acts 13:9]]

--- Abraham Fell upon His Face, and Laughed
kicker: vv. 17–19
sub: Thou Shalt Call His Name Isaac
scripture: Genesis 17:17-19 | mark: laughed; thou shalt call his name Isaac
p: And again, despite his deep faith and willingness to obey, Abraham was human, second guessing the power of God and His faithfulness to keep His promises. God assures Abraham that within the year Sarai, now Sarah, will bear a son, and he shall name him Isaac.

--- As for Ishmael
kicker: vv. 20–22
sub: But My Covenant Will I Establish with Isaac
scripture: Genesis 17:20-22 | mark: But my covenant will I establish with Isaac
p: To satisfy the prayer for Ishmael from Abraham, God says He will bless the elder son, from a bondwoman, but the elder will be blessed by the younger. And like Esau and Jacob, *the elder shall serve the younger*. [[Genesis 25:23]] [[lesson:genesis-16-hagar-and-ishmael|Genesis 16]]

=== The selfsame day
--- In the Selfsame Day
kicker: vv. 23–27
sub: Ishmael His Son Was Thirteen Years Old
scripture: Genesis 17:23-27 | mark: in the selfsame day; Ishmael his son was thirteen years old
p: Another lesson to take from this is how quickly Abraham obeys the {Lord} in something that seems crazy, I’m sure. But not only does he obey, he makes all the men of his household obey, including his 13 year old son.

--- Pray to Be a Father Like Abraham
kicker: Application • Genesis 17:23
sub: All the Men of His House
p: Parents today say things like, it’s so hard to get my teenager to not watch inappropriate material, or to dress modestly, or to go to church. Here Abraham is telling his 13 year old son that he’s got to cut off his foreskin, and not only the 13 year old son, but all the men of his house, including servants, herdsmen and slaves. [[Genesis 18:19]]

--- A Father Like Abraham
center: Abraham believed God and was saved long before the token of the covenant, and when God spoke, he obeyed in the selfsame day, and led his whole house to obey. Pray to be a father like Abraham.
